From d7df0a30ada086aa67892f262ba9b16f59d81fac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gilles Goetsch <code@gillesgoetsch.ch>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:59:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: apple: atc: Park the PIPE handler before a Type-C mode
 switch

When a DisplayPort alt mode device is hotplugged, the Type-C controller
calls the mux with the new mode while the USB3 data path is still live:
the PIPE handler is only parked by atcphy_dwc3_reset_assert(), and that
reset happens after the mux change, not before it. atcphy_mux_set() then
hits its WARN_ON_ONCE(atcphy->pipehandler_up)

    WARNING: drivers/phy/apple/atc.c:2328 at atcphy_mux_set+0x1010 [phy_apple_atc]
      typec_mux_set
      cd321x_update_work [tps6598x_core]

and atcphy_configure() reprograms the lanes underneath a running PIPE
handler. The hardware falls back to USB2 only and no DisplayPort link is
ever established, so a hotplugged monitor stays black while the same
monitor works when it is attached at boot.

Park the PIPE handler on the dummy PHY before switching modes, exactly as
atcphy_dwc3_reset_assert() does, so the lanes are quiet during the
switch. The subsequent dwc3 reset and set_mode bring USB3 back up as
before.

Tested on a MacBook Air (M2, 2022): hotplugging a DP alt mode display now
trains the link every time (22 modes reported on each plug) and the
warning no longer fires. The monitor's hub is USB 2.0, so USB3 operation
on the port after a hotplug has not been verified.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Gilles Goetsch <code@gillesgoetsch.ch>
---
 drivers/phy/apple/atc.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
index 9eb0a1d106ff93..767c1b38f186db 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
@@ -2264,6 +2264,7 @@ static int atcphy_mux_set(struct typec_mux_dev *mux, struct typec_mux_state *sta
 {
 	struct apple_atcphy *atcphy = typec_mux_get_drvdata(mux);
 	enum atcphy_mode target_mode;
+	int ret;
 
 	guard(mutex)(&atcphy->lock);
 
@@ -2321,11 +2322,28 @@ static int atcphy_mux_set(struct typec_mux_dev *mux, struct typec_mux_state *sta
 		return 0;
 
 	/*
-	 * If the pipehandler is still/already up here there's a bug somewhere so make sure to
-	 * complain loudly. We can still try to switch modes and hope for the best though,
-	 * in the worst case the hardware will fall back to USB2-only.
+	 * The Type-C controller reports an alt mode while the USB3 data path is
+	 * still live: the PIPE handler is only parked when dwc3 is reset, and
+	 * nothing forces a reset before the mux change. atcphy_configure() then
+	 * reprograms the lanes underneath a running PIPE handler, the hardware
+	 * falls back to USB2 and no DisplayPort link comes up at all -- which is
+	 * what happens when a DP monitor is hotplugged, while the same monitor
+	 * works when it is already attached at boot.
+	 *
+	 * Park the PIPE handler on the dummy PHY first, exactly as
+	 * atcphy_dwc3_reset_assert() does, so the lanes are quiet during the
+	 * switch. USB3 stays down until dwc3 reconfigures it; USB2 is unaffected.
 	 */
-	WARN_ON_ONCE(atcphy->pipehandler_up);
+	if (atcphy->pipehandler_up) {
+		ret = atcphy_configure_pipehandler_dummy(atcphy);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_warn(atcphy->dev,
+				 "Failed to park PIPE handler before mode switch: %d\n",
+				 ret);
+		else
+			atcphy->pipehandler_up = false;
+	}
+
 	return atcphy_configure(atcphy, target_mode);
 }
 
